{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_rate_calculus_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_rate_calculus_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L120-L205","doc":"**Surreal rate calculus — the four strict inequalities**\n([`prop:surreal-rate-calculus`]).\n\nWorking in an ordered field `F` carrying the rate data\n`[SurrealRateCalculus F]` (so the leading-coefficient equations\n`Δ = ε³`, `Ω · ε = 1`, … hold) and treating `ε` as a *strictly\npositive infinitesimal* — `0 < ε` together with `hε_inf`: every\npositive power `ε^(n+1)` lies below every standard real `λ > 0` —\nthe four claims of the proposition are **derived**, not assumed:\n\n1. **Positivity** — `0 < Δ` and `0 < Ω`.\n2. **Infinitesimal gap** — `Δ < λ` for every standard real `λ > 0`.\n3. **Transfinite period** — `λ < Ω` for every standard real `λ > 0`.\n4. **Squeeze** — `Δ < δ² · Ω` for every standard real `δ > 0`\n   (the mechanism underlying every millennium-problem squeeze:\n   a standard-scale cost `δ² · ε⁻¹` strictly exceeds the\n   infinitesimal dissipation `ε³`).\n\nThe proof is purely order-theoretic — items (1)–(3) follow from\nthe rate equations and the positivity/archimedean-smallness of\n`ε`; item (4) reduces, after multiplying by `ε > 0`, to\n`ε⁴ < δ²`, which is the `n = 3` instance of `hε_inf`.  No\ncancellation in an ordered field is possible because the cost is\ntransfinite and the dissipation infinitesimal.\n\n**The nine conjecture-cone binders were removed 2026-08-30.**  They were\n`{α : ℝ} {K ω : ℝ → ℝ} {Sbrk : Set ℝ}` together with `[QAubinLions K] …\n[RegularityBreakdown Sbrk]`, and the paragraph they replaced said plainly\nwhat they did: they *\"record the conditional dependency of the rate table\non the q-NS conjecture cone … the inequalities themselves are\nunconditional given the rate data and the infinitesimality of `ε`.\"*\n\nThat is an honest description of a dishonest signature.  A binder the\nproof never consumes does not record a dependency — it reads as one to\nanyone scanning the statement, while discharging nothing.  The proof below\nuses `S`, `hε_pos` and `hε_inf` and nothing else; four of the nine binders\nexisted only to supply parameters to the other five.\n\nThe dependency of the rate table on the cone is a manuscript-level claim\n(`conj:q-aubin-lions`, …, `conj:regularity-breakdown`) and belongs in the\n`.md` banner, which states it.  What is proved here is what the proof\nactually uses: the rate equations and the archimedean smallness of `ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surrealRateCalculus_classicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surrealRateCalculus_classicalLimit","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L78-L118","doc":"**Classical-limit model** (ε = 1).  Every rate quantity is `1`, so\nthree of the four rate equations degenerate to `1 = 1`:\n- `Δ = 1 = 1³`\n- `Ω · 1 = 1 · 1 = 1`\n- `Z³ · 1⁴ = 1 · 1 = 1`\n- `E(δ) · 1 = δ² · 1 = δ²` — the only field that still varies with\n  its argument, and only because `roguePartCost` is *defined* as\n  `fun δ => δ ^ 2`.\n\nThis is the \"no infinitesimal\" baseline: it fixes no rate ratio,\nbecause with `Δ = Ω = Z = 1` there are no ratios to fix.  The\nsubstantive content arises when `ε` is genuinely infinitesimal in\n`𝐍𝐨` via the standard-part embedding.\n\n**A `def`, not an `instance`, since 2026-08-24.**  The carrier was\nuniversally quantified (`(F : Type u) [CommRing F]`), so typeclass\nresolution supplied `ε = 1` for every commutative ring.\n`surreal_rate_calculus_conditional` below is stated over\n`[S : SurrealRateCalculus F]` and reads as conditional on the rate\ntable; with this instance in scope the class binder cost a caller\nnothing and the table it named was the all-ones one.\n\nWorth stating precisely, because it is *not* a vacuity claim about\nthat theorem: at `ε = 1` its other hypothesis `hε_inf` (`ε^(n+1)`\nbelow every positive `λ`) is unsatisfiable in an ordered field, so\nthe theorem cannot actually be *applied* at this model.  The defect\nis that the model is supplied silently — a reader of the signature\ncould not see which rate data the conclusion was about.\n\nCallers name it: `letI := surrealRateCalculus_classicalLimit F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.rogueZero_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.rogueZero_order","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Rogue-zero leading-coefficient equation:\n`E(δ) · ε = δ²` for every drift `δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.enstrophy_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.enstrophy_order","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Enstrophy leading-coefficient equation: `Z³ · ε⁴ = 1`\n(the cubic form of `Z = ε^(-4/3)`, avoiding fractional\nexponents at the type level). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.reebPeriod_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.reebPeriod_order","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Reeb-period leading-coefficient equation: `Ω · ε = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.massGap_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.massGap_order","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Mass-gap leading-coefficient equation: `Δ = ε³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.roguePartCost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.roguePartCost","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Rogue-zero energy cost, parametrised by a standard-real drift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.enstrophyCeiling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.enstrophyCeiling","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The enstrophy ceiling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.reebPeriod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.reebPeriod","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The Reeb period. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.massGap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.massGap","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The mass gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.epsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.epsilon","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The Reeb infinitesimal embedded in `F`.  Non-zero (forced\nby `reebPeriod_order : reebPeriod · epsilon = 1` below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus.mk","kind":"ctor","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SurrealRateCalculus","kind":"class","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/SurrealRateCalculus.lean#L40-L76","doc":"The rate-table *shape*: a class recording the four\nclassical-limit rates as data over an abstract field carrier `F`.\n\nAn instance of this class fixes the leading-coefficient equations\n`Δ = ε³`, `Ω·ε = 1`, `Z³·ε⁴ = 1`, `E(δ)·ε = δ²` (each up to a\npositive scalar absorbed into the named quantity) and entails\nthe rate table [`prop:surreal-rate-calculus`].  Under the surreal\nembedding `ε ↦ 1/ω`, these equations specialise to the\n`Ow`-valuations `Ow(Δ) = -3`, `Ow(Ω) = 1`, `Ow(Z) = 4/3`,\n`Ow(E(δ)) = 1` whenever `δ ≠ 0` (the rogue-zero equation\n`E(δ)·ε = δ²` holds for every `δ : F`; the `Ow = 1`\ninterpretation requires `δ ≠ 0`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:surreal-rate-calculus","label":"prop:surreal-rate-calculus","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-rate-calculus.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}